well joining us now is the mayor of  london at sadiq khan uh thank you very  much for being on the program and mr  khan what's your response to last trust  as victory  well on a personal level i sincerely  congratulate liz trust and being elected  the conservative leader today  she'll be the prime minister uh tomorrow  we may come from different political  traditions but she was a councillor in  london between 2006 and 2010. i'm hoping  that uh what unites us  is our common desire to see a capital  city flourishing and thriving but also  our country succeeding  do you think she's a person that you  could work with  we need to  we need to put aside a part of little  difference  we need to avoid this anti-london stuff  we've seen over the last two three years  we need to avoid pitching communities  and people against one another  because of a culture wall and work  together to address saw and inflation to  work together to address the rise in  energy prices work together to keep the  head above water of those families those  communities those businesses that are  looking to the prime minister and myself  for leadership and working together  just to come in what what do you mean by  could anti-london a sort of rhetoric  that we've seen you talk about the  leveling up agenda there  well look some people perceive  leveling up as meaning  making london poorer that certainly is  one way to make our country more level i  think it's nonsensical particularly when  before the pandemic we as the capital  city contributed net 40 billion pounds  to the treasury which is then  distributed around the country for  example our public transport in london  suffered hugely because londoners did  the right thing and stayed at home so we  need support from the government in the  short term to make sure public transport  works in london that ensures our  businesses can have workers get into  their offices and tourists getting  around our city it makes no sense to  punish londoners by solving tfl of  support and there are other examples of  pots of funding from the government that  we are able to bid for so what i'm  saying is look i understand the  importance of making our country more  equal one of the ways of doing that is  by devolving more powers and resources  to manchester to liverpool to sheffield  sheffield and london so we can all you  know flourish and thrive rather than  london struggling and as a consequence  our country's struggling too i spoke to  west streeting the shadow health  secretary a little bit earlier on this  afternoon and he told me that he would  like to see liz trust call an election  but she doesn't have a mandate she can't  break away  from the manifesto in a democratic way  without calling an election do you agree  with that well if this trust is going to  be continuity of boris johnson then i  think the british public deserve the  opportunity to vote for a fresh start  under key osama and the labour party  many of the issues that are causing this  national crisis have been exacerbated by  the government of the last 12 years look  at these strikes which are a symptom of  12 years of austerity where those in the  public sector in particular have seen  peka after paco over the last 12 years  look at the cost of energy in the uk  versus the cost of energy in the  european union and across the world so  look if list trust is continuity boris  johnson  to theresa may then i think we do need a  general election to give the british  public the option of a fresh start under  cure some with fresh different policies  or continuation of the conservatives  which we've seen over the last 12 years  causing real problems around the country  boris johnson was an election winner  wasn't he do you think that he would  have been a more formidable opponent  than liz trust  well he's the past  i'm keen to talk about the future  and liz trust is the future prime  minister of our country from tomorrow i  want to reset relations between me the  mayor of london and the mayor of the  capital city uh and the the new prime  minister i think what we need to do is  to stop seeing north versus south or  older versus younger or one faith versus  another what we want to see what we  deserve is a prime minister governor in  the national interest rather than  governing in the narrow part of  political interest  okay uh mayor of london thank you very  much indeed for being on the program  today
 

